This section provides detailed API documentation for all LINE Solver MATLAB modules.

@section api_overview Overview

The LINE Solver MATLAB API is organized into several categories:

- @subpage api_core - Essential classes for building queueing models: networks, nodes, job classes,
  distributions, solvers, and layered networks.

- @subpage api_utilities - Helper functions, constants, and enumerations.

<b>Algorithm Modules:</b>

- @subpage api_pfqn - MVA, convolution, and normalizing constant methods
- @subpage api_cache - Cache performance analysis
- @subpage api_mam - QBD processes and matrix-analytic solutions
- @subpage api_qsys - Single-station queueing system analysis
- @subpage api_sn - Network analysis and transformation utilities
- @subpage api_mc - CTMC and DTMC analysis tools

<b>Specialized Modules:</b>

- @subpage api_polling - Analysis of gated, exhaustive, and k-limited polling
- @subpage api_npfqn - Approximations for intractable queueing networks
- @subpage api_lossn - Analysis of networks with blocking
- @subpage api_lsn - Layered queueing network analysis
- @subpage api_rl - RL utilities for queueing control

